      "content": "Answer the following question with a single MySQL SQL query against the current database. Explore the semantic network and verify with mysql_query as needed. The SELECT list must contain exactly the columns the question asks for, in the asked order. When the final SQL is verified, call the submit_SQL tool with it.\n\nThe following hints are provided to help you write the SQL:\n\n## Gold Tables\n- FCLT_ROOMS\n- FCLT_BUILDING_HIST\n- FCLT_BUILDING\n\n## Column Mapping\n- academic building: FCLT_BUILDING.BUILDING_TYPE\n- owned by MIT: FCLT_BUILDING.OWNERSHIP_TYPE, FCLT_BUILDING.SITE\n- excluding the Stata building: FCLT_BUILDING.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY\n- building name: FCLT_BUILDING.BUILDING_NAME\n- fiscal period: FCLT_BUILDING_HIST.FISCAL_PERIOD\n- total area of rooms used for \"RESIDENT\" or \"LABS\" purposes: FCLT_ROOMS.AREA, FCLT_ROOMS.MAJOR_USE_DESC\n- total room area greater than 1000: FCLT_ROOMS.AREA\n- assignable area: FCLT_BUILDING_HIST.ASSIGNABLE_AREA\n- campus sector: FCLT_BUILDING.CAMPUS_SECTOR\n- external gross area: FCLT_BUILDING.EXT_GROSS_AREA\n\n## Join Keys\n- FCLT_BUILDING_HIST.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY <-> FCLT_ROOMS.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY\n- FCLT_BUILDING.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY <-> FCLT_BUILDING_HIST.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY\n\n## Domain Knowledge\n- \"academic building\" is predicated by \"TABLE.BUILDING_TYPE = 'ACADEMIC'\"\n- \"owned\" is predicated by \"TABLE.OWNERSHIP_TYPE = 'OWNED'\"\n- \"buildings at MIT\" is predicated by \"TABLE.SITE = 'MIT'\"\n- \"owned\" is predicated by \"TABLE.OWNERSHIP_TYPE = 'OWNED'\"\n- \"Stata building\" is predicated by \"TABLE.BUILDING_KEY = '32'\"\n\n## Subquery Decomposition\n1. For each building, give the building name and calculate the total area of rooms used for \"RESIDENT\" or \"LABS\" purposes, considering only buildings with a total room area greater than 1000, and only include buildings that are classified as \"academic buildings\" and are owned by MIT.\n```sql\nSELECT fb.BUILDING_NAME, SUM(fr.AREA) AS total_room_area FROM FCLT_ROOMS fr JOIN FCLT_BUILDING fb ON fr.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY = fb.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY WHERE fr.MAJOR_USE_DESC IN ('RESIDENT', 'LABS') AND fb.BUILDING_TYPE = 'ACADEMIC' AND fb.OWNERSHIP_TYPE = 'OWNED' GROUP BY fb.BUILDING_NAME HAVING total_room_area > 1000 ;\n```\n2. For academic buildings at MIT, show the building key, building name, fiscal period, and the running sum of assignable area within each campus sector, but only include buildings that are owned, and exclude the Stata building. Order the results by building key.\n```sql\nSELECT fb.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY, fb.BUILDING_NAME, fbh.FISCAL_PERIOD, SUM(fbh.ASSIGNABLE_AREA) OVER (PARTITION BY fb.CAMPUS_SECTOR ORDER BY fb.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY, fbh.FISCAL_PERIOD ROWS BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW) AS running_assignable_area FROM FCLT_BUILDING fb JOIN FCLT_BUILDING_HIST fbh ON fb.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY = fbh.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY WHERE fb.BUILDING_TYPE = 'ACADEMIC' AND fb.SITE = 'MIT' AND fb.OWNERSHIP_TYPE = 'OWNED' AND fb.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY <> '32' ORDER BY fb.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY, fbh.FISCAL_PERIOD;\n```\n3. For each building, provide the building name, the fiscal period, and the total area of rooms used for \"RESIDENT\" or \"LABS\" purposes, considering only buildings with a total room area greater than 1000, and only include buildings that are classified as \"academic buildings\" and are owned by MIT. For each fiscal period, include a grand total for all buildings in the format of (null, fiscal period, total room area).\n```sql\nWITH inner_cte AS ( SELECT fb.BUILDING_NAME, SUM(fr.AREA) AS total_room_area, fb.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY FROM FCLT_ROOMS fr JOIN FCLT_BUILDING fb ON fr.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY = fb.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY WHERE fr.MAJOR_USE_DESC IN ('RESIDENT', 'LABS') AND fb.BUILDING_TYPE = 'ACADEMIC' AND fb.OWNERSHIP_TYPE = 'OWNED' GROUP BY fb.BUILDING_NAME, fb.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY HAVING SUM(fr.AREA) > 1000 ), BuildingPeriods AS ( SELECT ic.BUILDING_NAME, fbh.FISCAL_PERIOD, ic.total_room_area FROM inner_cte ic JOIN FCLT_BUILDING_HIST fbh ON ic.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY = fbh.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY ) SELECT bp.BUILDING_NAME, bp.FISCAL_PERIOD, SUM(bp.total_room_area) AS total_room_area FROM BuildingPeriods bp GROUP BY bp.FISCAL_PERIOD, bp.BUILDING_NAME WITH ROLLUP HAVING SUM(bp.total_room_area) > 0 ORDER BY bp.FISCAL_PERIOD, bp.BUILDING_NAME\n```\n4. For academic buildings at MIT, show the building key, building name, fiscal period, and the running sum of assignable area within each campus sector, but only include buildings that are owned, and exclude the Stata building. Also, for each result, include the building's external gross area from the FCLT_BUILDING table. Order the results by building key and fiscal period.\n```sql\nWITH inner_cte AS ( SELECT fb.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY, fb.BUILDING_NAME, fbh.FISCAL_PERIOD, SUM(fbh.ASSIGNABLE_AREA) OVER (PARTITION BY fb.CAMPUS_SECTOR ORDER BY fb.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY, fbh.FISCAL_PERIOD ROWS BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW) AS running_assignable_area FROM FCLT_BUILDING fb JOIN FCLT_BUILDING_HIST fbh ON fb.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY = fbh.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY WHERE fb.BUILDING_TYPE = 'ACADEMIC' AND fb.SITE = 'MIT' AND fb.OWNERSHIP_TYPE = 'OWNED' AND fb.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY <> '32' ) SELECT icte.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY, icte.BUILDING_NAME, icte.FISCAL_PERIOD, icte.running_assignable_area, fb.EXT_GROSS_AREA FROM inner_cte icte JOIN FCLT_BUILDING fb ON icte.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY = fb.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY ORDER BY icte.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY, icte.FISCAL_PERIOD;\n```\n\n## Question\nFor each academic building at MIT that is owned by MIT (excluding the Stata building), and for each fiscal period, provide the building name, the fiscal period, the total area of rooms used for \"RESIDENT\" or \"LABS\" purposes (considering only buildings with a total room area greater than 1000), the running sum of assignable area within each campus sector, and the building's external gross area. Only include buildings classified as academic buildings and owned by MIT. Order the results by fiscal period and building name. Do not return any rounded answers."
